## 7. Error and boundary matrix

### [CXC-LTW-BOUNDARIES] Every condition a builder would otherwise have to invent an answer for

| # | Condition | Required behaviour |
|---|-----------|--------------------|
| 1 | `emit` round trip holds | write; report on the receipt |
| 2 | `emit` round trip fails on a property value | REFUSE; name node id, property key, expected value, parsed value, first divergent byte offset ([CXC-LTW-EMIT-REFUSE]) |
| 3 | `emit` round trip fails because the content is not expressible in the current format | REFUSE with a DISTINGUISHABLE reason code — never collapsed into the malformed-content error |
| 4 | `emit` asked to write an id already present in the target corpus | REFUSE; a duplicate id is never a merge |
| 5 | `emit` output would introduce a NEW dangling reference | REPORT on the receipt, do not refuse — unless the caller selected STRICT guard mode, which refuses and rolls back ([CXC-LTW-CALLERS]) |
| 6 | `emit` given a value containing embedded newlines | collapse each newline run to ONE space, emit on one physical line, compare the round trip against the COLLAPSED input ([CXC-LTW-SHAPE] S1) |
| 7 | `emit` given a value longer than any line-length preference | emit it on one line; there is no line-length limit and one MUST NOT be added |
| 8 | `emit` called twice with the same content | byte-identical output; no timestamp, hostname or dict-order leakage ([CXC-LTW-EMITTER]) |
| 9 | `rewrite` with an EMPTY transformation set | return the input byte-identical; no implicit clean-up |
| 10 | `rewrite` with an unrecognized transformation name | REFUSE listing the five valid names; never silently ignore |
| 11 | `rewrite` where two selected transformations target the same line | REFUSE naming the line and both transformations; never a silent precedence |
| 12 | `rewrite` level-1 graph superset fails | leave the file byte-identical; receipt `written: false`, `verdict_level_1: fail` with the failing axis named |
| 13 | `rewrite` level-1 passes and level-2 line accounting fails | leave the file byte-identical; receipt names EVERY `dropped` line — this is the prohibited-implementation signature ([CXC-LTW-NO-ROUNDTRIP]) |
| 14 | either verdict cannot be computed | verdict is `not-run`, NEVER `pass`; file left untouched |
| 15 | `rewrite(rewrite(f)) != rewrite(f)` | FAIL the pass, leave the file untouched, name the transformation and the first differing byte offset; never iterate to a fixed point ([CXC-LTW-IDEMPOTENT]) |
| 16 | `unwrap-property` meets an indented line it cannot classify as continuation or structure | leave the property untouched; REPORT as unclassified; never guess |
| 17 | `unwrap-property` meets an indented block that is a nested mapping, a nested list, or a code block | not a target; leave it entirely alone |
| 18 | `hoist-root-id` meets a bare-line id whose tag is unregistered | REFUSE; a repair MUST NOT invent a tag ([SPEC:LTS-DOC-ROOT]) |
| 19 | `hoist-root-id` meets a bare line with a trailing description | the description becomes the blockquote summary after the h1; discarding it is a `dropped` line and fails level 2 |
| 20 | `add-frontmatter` with no caller-supplied `scope` / `audience` / `boundary` | REFUSE; never invent a value, never write a placeholder |
| 21 | `suggest-elements` | SUGGEST ONLY, never write; emit the suggestion together with the widen-it statement ([DRI-ELEMENTS-INTENT]) |
| 22 | a corpus run in which `suggest-elements` values were written automatically | treat the run as UNVALIDATED, not clean — a control fitted to its own result |
| 23 | `add-part-of` on the document root, or on a bracketless section divider | not a target; leave alone |
| 24 | a caller needs a shape the library does not emit | raise a spec amendment; never format the line locally, never post-process library output ([CXC-LTW-ONE-WRITER]) |
| 25 | a second `.lts` emitter appears anywhere in the tree | refused at review; the grep is an acceptance criterion (LTW-C12) |
| 26 | implementation begins before the parser fix has landed | BLOCKED; the behavioural parser-fix fixture (LTW-C0) must pass first, and a version check is not a substitute ([CXC-LTW-PARSER-DEP]) |
| 27 | any proposal to implement `rewrite` as `emit(parse(f))`, by any composition | REFUSED at review, not at test — the test that would catch it is the test the defect satisfies ([CXC-LTW-NO-ROUNDTRIP]) |
| 28 | a caller asks the rewriter to REORDER properties or sections, by name or by flag | REFUSE — `reorder` is not a member of the closed transformation set; David ruled transform-in-place 2026-08-11 ([DD-LTW-REORDER]) and adding it is a spec amendment, not a configuration |
| 29 | a caller passes `content` in anything other than the parser's node model — a richer authoring type, or a type requiring a lowering step | REFUSE at review; the input type is the parser's model and there is no projection in the call path ([DD-LTW-INPUT-TYPE], [CXC-LTW-EMITTER]) |
| 30 | `emit` refuses for any reason | the refusal is emitted as a structured event with its reason code to `{corpus}/events/quality.jsonl`; an unrecorded refusal leaves [DD-LTW-INPUT-TYPE]'s `invalidating_assumption` untestable ([CXC-LTW-EMIT-REFUSE]) |

- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-LTS-WRITER]

