## 8. Acceptance — two tiers, machine and glass

### [CXC-LTW-ACCEPT] Every requirement has a machine signal; every operator-facing surface has a glass gate

- rule: a machine signal certifies the emission, the transformation and the verdict. Anything whose value is an OPERATOR reading a diff or a receipt also needs a glass gate, because a migration that is technically verified and practically unreviewable is how a bulk edit ships unread.

| ID | Requirement | `verify.machine` | `verify.human` (glass) |
|----|-------------|------------------|------------------------|
| LTW-C0 | **BLOCKING — the parser fix is present, measured behaviourally** ([CXC-LTW-PARSER-DEP]) | `tests/test_lts_writer_deps.py::test_wrapped_continuation_survives_parse` — a fixture whose wrapped property value parses back in FULL; the build MUST NOT proceed past a failure, and a version check is not a substitute | — |
| LTW-C1 | **`parse(emit(x)) == x` holds on every emission** ([CXC-LTW-EMITTER]) | `tests/test_lts_emitter.py::test_round_trip_property_based` — property-based over generated content including long values, embedded newlines, unicode, every registered edge verb, and every frontmatter key | — |
| LTW-C2 | **A round-trip failure REFUSES and names the part** ([CXC-LTW-EMIT-REFUSE]) | `::test_refusal_names_node_key_expected_actual_offset` — inject a truncating stub; assert no file is written, no text returned, and all five fields present on a typed error | an operator shown one refusal can locate the offending content without opening the writer's source |
| LTW-C3 | Not-yet-expressible is DISTINGUISHABLE from malformed ([CXC-LTW-EMIT-REFUSE]) | `::test_inexpressible_has_distinct_reason_code` — assert the two refusals carry different codes | — |
| LTW-C4 | The emitter is PURE ([CXC-LTW-EMITTER]) | `::test_emission_is_byte_stable` — same content emitted 100 times under shuffled dict order yields one distinct output | — |
| LTW-C5 | **`parse(rewrite(f)) ⊇ parse(f)` on every rewritten file** ([CXC-LTW-REWRITER]) | `tests/test_lts_rewriter.py::test_graph_superset_over_whole_corpus` — every `.lts` under `corpora/`, every transformation, asserting nodes, edges, property keys and value-lengths never shrink | — |
| LTW-C6 | **⛔ THE GATE — the prohibited implementation FAILS level 2** ([CXC-LTW-NO-ROUNDTRIP], [CXC-LTW-VERIFY]) | `::test_parse_then_emit_passes_level_1_and_fails_level_2` — implement `emit(parse(f))` AS A FIXTURE, run it on `57-substrate-agnostic-subscription-filtering.lts`, assert level 1 PASSES and level 2 reports the dropped lines. A harness that cannot fail this way cannot detect the defect this spec exists to prevent | the architect reads the level-2 report for that fixture and confirms it names the lost content rather than a count |
| LTW-C7 | Line accounting admits NO `dropped` ([CXC-LTW-VERIFY]) | `::test_dropped_line_fails_rewrite` — a deliberately truncating transformation is rejected, the file is unchanged, and the finding names the input line number and content | — |
| LTW-C8 | `merged` and `relocated` are proved by VERBATIM containment | `::test_disposition_requires_verbatim_containment` — a near-miss (one character changed) is `dropped`, not `merged`; no similarity score anywhere in the path | — |
| LTW-C9 | **Byte-level idempotence, checked in every RUN not only in tests** ([CXC-LTW-IDEMPOTENT]) | `::test_idempotent_over_whole_corpus` — every file, every transformation, byte equality on the second application; plus `::test_run_performs_its_own_idempotence_check` asserting the receipt carries the field | — |
| LTW-C10 | Per-transformation independence and order-freedom ([CXC-LTW-TRANSFORMS]) | `::test_transformations_commute` — every permutation of every selected subset yields byte-identical output; `::test_single_transformation_touches_only_its_targets` | an operator runs `unwrap-property` alone over the corpus and the diff contains only unwrapped properties |
| LTW-C11 | **`suggest-elements` NEVER writes** ([CXC-LTW-TRANSFORMS], [DRI-ELEMENTS-INTENT]) | `::test_suggest_elements_does_not_write` — assert the file is byte-identical and the suggestion is returned with the widen-it statement in the same output | — |
| LTW-C12 | **No second emitter anywhere in the tree** ([CXC-LTW-ONE-WRITER]) | `tests/test_one_writer.py::test_no_second_emitter` — grep the tree for `.lts` line-formatting outside the library (`### [`, `- {k}: `, `---` frontmatter assembly, Relationships triple assembly) and assert the only hits are the library and its tests | — |
| LTW-C13 | The absorption is behaviour-preserving ([CXC-LTW-ONE-WRITER]) | `decision_ops`' and `defect_ops`' existing suites pass UNCHANGED against the library, and `project_validator`'s render -> parse -> validate selftest passes against the library call | David's live decision graph takes a real write through the migrated path and reads back correctly |
| LTW-C14 | The receipt is complete and auditable ([CXC-LTW-RECEIPT]) | `::test_receipt_has_every_field_for_every_file` — including files left unchanged; assert `not-run` is never serialized as `pass`; assert the JSONL lands in `{corpus}/events/quality.jsonl` | an operator reads one receipt and can answer what was requested, what was applied, what was recovered and why a skipped file was skipped |
| LTW-C15 | An unprovable `⊇` leaves the file UNTOUCHED ([CXC-LTW-RECEIPT]) | `::test_unproven_file_is_not_written` — for each of the four failure modes, assert the file bytes are unchanged and the receipt records `written: false` with the reason; assert no override flag exists | — |
| LTW-C16 | Canonical form is DERIVED, not invented ([CXC-LTW-CANONICAL-DERIVED]) | `tests/test_canonical_form.py::test_emitter_reproduces_conformant_file` — round-trip `29-composeux-embedded-reactive.lts` through the emitter and assert every difference is attributable to a numbered rule in [CXC-LTW-SHAPE] | a reviewer diffs an emitted file against a hand-authored conformant one and cannot tell which is which |
| LTW-C17 | This document round-trips ([CXC-LTW-SHAPE] dogfooding) | `::test_spec_59_round_trips` — parse this file, emit it, assert graph equality and that no property value in the emitted output spans more than one physical line | — |
| LTW-C18 | The corpus recovery is MEASURED against the baseline ([CXC-LTW-RECEIPT]) | `::test_corpus_unwrap_recovers_expected_characters` — a full `unwrap-property` pass reports total `characters_recovered` within a stated tolerance of the 148,847-character baseline; a much smaller number means files were silently skipped | David reads the run summary and confirms the headline number against the census |
| LTW-C19 | **The rewriter does NOT reorder** ([DD-LTW-REORDER], [CXC-LTW-REWRITER]) | `tests/test_lts_rewriter.py::test_no_transformation_reorders` — for every file and every transformation other than `hoist-root-id`, assert the input line numbers of the `retained` and `merged` output lines form a STRICTLY INCREASING sequence; plus `::test_no_reorder_transformation_exists` asserting the transformation registry has exactly the five names and that an explicit `reorder` request is REFUSED, not ignored | an operator diffs a full migration pass and every hunk is attributable to a named transformation's target lines; `git blame` on an unrelated property line is unchanged |
| LTW-C20 | **The emitter's input type IS the parser's node model** ([DD-LTW-INPUT-TYPE], [CXC-LTW-EMITTER]) | `tests/test_lts_emitter.py::test_input_type_is_parser_node_model` — assert `emit` accepts the object `factlattice.parse()` returns with NO adapter and NO lowering step, and that the round-trip comparison in the call path is a direct structural equality with no projection function between the two sides | — |
| LTW-C21 | Refusals are RECORDED, not merely raised ([CXC-LTW-EMIT-REFUSE], [DD-LTW-INPUT-TYPE]) | `::test_refusal_is_emitted_as_a_quality_event` — assert every refusal appends one JSONL event carrying its reason code to `{corpus}/events/quality.jsonl`, and that the set is aggregable by reason code without parsing prose | David or the architect reads the accumulated refusal set periodically — this reading is the named condition on which [DD-LTW-INPUT-TYPE] rests, and its absence is what would reopen that decision |

- requirement: **LTW-C0, LTW-C6, LTW-C9 and LTW-C15 are the gates.** LTW-C0 is blocking and external — a build that starts without it certifies the truncation as intent. **LTW-C6 is the criterion that protects every other measurement in this spec**: it requires the harness to demonstrate, on the real file, that it can DETECT the prohibited implementation, and a harness that cannot fail that way is one that will report clean on a corpus reduced to 18% of itself. A build failing LTW-C9 has produced a migration that cannot be safely re-run. A build failing LTW-C15 has produced a tool that writes files it could not verify, which is the hand-typing it replaced with a machine's confidence attached.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-LTS-WRITER]

